BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bar-call-request-for-proposals-2027-dewey-square-activation@boston-art-
 map
DTSTAMP:20261125T000106Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:Deadline: Request for Proposals: 2027 Dewey Square Activation
DESCRIPTION:The Greenway Conservancy seeks an entrepreneurial partner to en
 vision\, design\, build\, install\, manage\, and operate a vibrant outdoor
  activation in Dewey Square Park. The activation may take the form of an o
 utdoor concession\, bar\, kiosk\, café\, retail pop-up shop\, market\, ac
 tivity\, event or performance series\, or other innovative concept that br
 ings people together and enhances the experience of the plaza and surround
 ing district.\nhttps://www.rosekennedygreenway.org/wp-content/uploads/2026
 /10/2027-Dewey-Square-RFP-FINAL.pdf
URL:https://www.rosekennedygreenway.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/2027-Dew
 ey-Square-RFP-FINAL.pdf
CATEGORIES:Open call
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bar-call-open-call-public-art-for-spatial-justice@boston-art-map
DTSTAMP:20261125T000106Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:Deadline: Open Call: Public Art for Spatial Justice
DESCRIPTION:NEFA's Public Art for Spatial Justice grants range from $15\,00
 0 to $30\,000 for up to a two-year grant period\, starting March 2027. Pro
 jects must take place in Massachusetts and creatively cultivate expression
 s or embodiments of spatial justice through public art-making. All artisti
 c disciplines are welcome to apply.\nhttps://www.nefa.org/CreateSpatialJus
 tice
URL:https://www.nefa.org/CreateSpatialJustice
CATEGORIES:Open call
END:VEVENT
